   "attributes": {
    "title": "CME 299:  Engineering Your Career Path — Career Readiness Workshops for Graduate Students",
    "path": {
     "alias": "/events/career-forum-education/cme-299-engineering-your-career-path-career-readiness-workshops",
     "pid": 8396,
     "langcode": "en"
    },
    "body": "<p>In today's competitive economy, developing professional skills is essential for thriving in graduate school and beyond. This six-week workshop series brings together career experts, recruiters, hiring managers, Stanford alumni, and fellow students to share practical advice and strategies for navigating your career. Workshops cover resumes and interviewing, networking, navigating the hiring process, using AI in your job search, presenting with impact, salary and position negotiation, and more. Each session offers practical tools and insights you can apply to your career development and professional journey.&nbsp;<br><br>Enrollment limited to ICME and Statistics graduate students. Recommended for first-years &amp; those nearing graduation. Questions or Other Stanford SOE graduate students interested in enrolling should contact Tanya Schornack at <a href=\"mailto:contact@example.com\">contact@example.com</a>.</p>",
