   "attributes": {
    "title": "Industry Insider: AI & Computer Vision with Reza Zadeh, PhD ’13 (ICME alum), Founder & CEO of Matroid",
    "path": {
     "alias": "/events/career-forum-education/industry-insider-ai-computer-vision-reza-zadeh-phd-13-icme-alum",
     "pid": 8681,
     "langcode": "en"
    },
    "body": "<p>Get to Know Matroid at ICME! Hear from <a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/rezab/\">Stanford ICME alum Reza Zadeh</a>, the founder of Matroid, who will share insights into the company's mission, culture, department focus, and the computer vision technologies powering its work.&nbsp;</p><div class=\"align-right media-entity-wrapper image\">\n  \n  \n\n\n\n\n            <div class=\"media image field-media-image label-hidden\">  <img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/sites/g/files/sbiybj17116/files/styles/stanford_circle/public/media/image/reza_zadeh_1.jpg.png?itok=RKkRrO9U\" width=\"140\" height=\"140\" alt>\n\n\n</div>\n      \n</div>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/rezab/\"><strong>Reza Zadeh</strong></a><strong> is the founder and CEO of Matroid, a computer vision company that enables users to build and deploy detectors without writing code. He is also an Adjunct Professor at Stanford University, where his research focuses on machine learning and distributed computing. A Stanford ICME alum, Reza previously served as a Consulting Professor at Stanford and a technical advisor to Databricks. His work bridges cutting-edge research and industry applications, with a focus on making advanced AI accessible and impactful.</strong><br><br>Learn more about <a href=\"https://www.matroid.com/\">Matroid</a>.</p><p><em>Please note that this event is for Stanford students. Snacks will be provided. If you have any questions, please get in touch with ICME Career Services:&nbsp;</em><a href=\"mailto:contact@example.com\"><em>Tanya Schornack</em></a><br><br>&nbsp;</p>",
