   "attributes": {
    "title": "Industry Insider: Mathematical Frontiers, ML & the Future of Energy with SLB",
    "path": {
     "alias": "/events/career-forum-education/industry-insider-mathematical-frontiers-ml-future-energy-slb",
     "pid": 8686,
     "langcode": "en"
    },
    "body": "<p>Join us for this special<strong> Industry Insider with SLB!</strong></p><ul><li>Explore the intersection of mathematics, machine learning, and fluid dynamics.</li><li>Learn how ML can accelerate optimal control and reservoir simulation.</li><li>Discover approaches to improve sample efficiency and model reliability.</li><li>See how reinforcement learning enables risk-aware control and inverse problems.</li><li>Learn about careers and opportunities at SLB.</li></ul><p>Learn more about <a href=\"https://www.slb.com/\">SLB</a>.<br><br><strong>Featured Guests:</strong></p><div class=\"align-left media-entity-wrapper image\">\n  \n  \n\n\n\n\n            <div class=\"media image field-media-image label-hidden\">  <img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/sites/g/files/sbiybj17116/files/styles/stanford_circle/public/media/image/rodneylessard_0.jpg.png?itok=fwJrUVb0\" width=\"140\" height=\"140\" alt>\n\n\n</div>\n      \n</div>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/lessardrw/\">Rodney Lessard</a>, Scientific Computing and Modelling Lead, SLB Software Technology Innovation Center&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><div class=\"align-left media-entity-wrapper image\">\n  \n  \n\n\n\n\n            <div class=\"media image field-media-image label-hidden\">  <img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/sites/g/files/sbiybj17116/files/styles/stanford_circle/public/media/image/suryasathujoda_1.jpg.png?itok=EGUP2Yc8\" width=\"140\" height=\"140\" alt>\n\n\n</div>\n      \n</div>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/suryasathujoda/\">Surya Sathujoda</a>, Data Scientist, SLB Software Technology Innovation Center&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Full Title &amp; Abstract</strong><br><strong>Mathematical Frontiers in Machine Learning for Fluid Dynamics: Risk-Aware Control and Inverse Problems</strong><br>In this talk, we examine the mathematical intersection of partial differential equations (PDEs), numerical analysis, and machine learning (ML) within fluid dynamics and reservoir simulation. While classical solvers provide rigorous physical accuracy, their high evaluation cost within iterative loops for high-dimensional optimal control and history matching motivates the adoption of ML architectures. Deploying ML in these highly non-linear, multi-scale regimes introduces a new set of challenges: standard models suffer from severe sample inefficiency and lack generalization guarantees outside their training manifold. To resolve these limitations, we highlight frontiers that exploit the mathematical structure of the physics: utilizing geometric deep learning to preserve fundamental symmetries and improve sample efficiency, and deploying probabilistic frameworks for rigorous, out-of-distribution confidence bounds. Finally, we discuss how these elements enable Reinforcement Learning (RL) for robust, risk-aware control and inverse problems.</p><p><em>Please note that this event is for Stanford students.&nbsp;Lunch will be provided. If you have any questions, please get in touch with ICME Career Services:&nbsp;</em><a href=\"mailto:contact@example.com\"><em>Tanya Schornack</em></a><br><br>&nbsp;</p>",
