   "attributes": {
    "title": "Industry Insider: Cerebras | Rethinking the Speed of AI",
    "path": {
     "alias": "/events/career-forum-education/industry-insider-cerebras-rethinking-speed-ai",
     "pid": 8711,
     "langcode": "en"
    },
    "body": "<p><strong>What happens when AI can respond almost as fast as you can think?</strong></p><p>Join <strong>Cerebras Systems</strong> for an inside look at how the company is rethinking AI computing and building technology designed to make AI dramatically faster. Learn how Cerebras is approaching the challenges of AI at scale and what faster inference could mean for the next generation of AI applications.</p><p><strong>Founded by Stanford alum Andrew Feldman</strong>, Cerebras is building the future of AI infrastructure through its innovative wafer-scale computing technology. Feldman is the company’s co-founder and CEO and holds both an MBA and BA from Stanford.</p><p>For Stanford students interested in AI, machine learning, computing, and technology, this is an opportunity to hear directly from the team building the future of AI and learn more about internship and full-time career opportunities at Cerebras.</p><p>Learn more about Cerebras Systems: <a href=\"https://www.cerebras.ai/\">https://www.cerebras.ai/</a></p><p><em>Please note that this event is for Stanford students.&nbsp;Lunch will be provided. If you have any questions, please get in touch with ICME Career Services:&nbsp;</em><a href=\"mailto:contact@example.com\"><em>Tanya Schornack</em></a><br><br>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br><br>&nbsp;</p>",
