   "attributes": {
    "title": "ICME Career Forum 2026",
    "path": {
     "alias": "/events/career-forum-education/icme-career-forum-2026",
     "pid": 7976,
     "langcode": "en"
    },
    "body": "<p>The <a href=\"https://icme.stanford.edu/get-involved/annual-events-icme/xtend-career-forum\">ICME Career Forum</a> is a one-of-a-kind event that brings together MS and PhD students from ICME and other related programs with our <a href=\"https://icme.stanford.edu/corporate-programs\">I</a><a href=\"https://icme.stanford.edu/Affiliate-Program\">CME Affiliates</a> from industry and national labs for a day of networking and recruiting. Unlike any other career event offered on campus, the ICME Career Forum connects students and hiring managers with each other in a relaxed and personal setting that you won't find at large-scale career fairs. <br><br><strong>EVENT DETAILS &amp; FAQS</strong><br><a href=\"https://icme.stanford.edu/icme-career-forum-information-organizations\"><strong>For Organizations</strong></a><br><a href=\"https://icme.stanford.edu/icme-career-forum-information-students\"><strong>For Students</strong></a><br><br><strong>SAMPLE AGENDA FOR THURSDAY, NOVEMBER 5, 2026</strong></p><table class=\"table\"><tbody><tr><td>Starts at 8:30 AM</td><td><strong>Check-in and Name Badge Pick-up (Huang Basement near Nvidia Auditorium)</strong></td></tr><tr><td>9:00 - 10:30 AM</td><td><strong>Morning Meet &amp; Greet: Students and Organizations</strong></td></tr><tr><td>10:30 AM - 12:30 PM </td><td><strong>Pre-Scheduled Interviews/Open Houses</strong></td></tr><tr><td>12:30 - 1:30 PM</td><td><strong>Afternoon Break</strong></td></tr><tr><td>1:30 - 4:00 PM</td><td><strong>Pre-Scheduled Interviews/Open Houses</strong></td></tr><tr><td>4:00 - 5:00 PM</td><td><strong>Bonus Interviews for Students</strong></td></tr></tbody></table><p><em>If you have any questions, please contact Tanya Schornack, ICME Program Manager of Affiliates &amp; Career Services, at </em><a href=\"mailto:tschorna@stahford.edu\"><em>contact@example.com</em></a>.<br><br> </p><p> </p>",
